---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { toolsByCategory } from '../../lib/tools';
import { collectionPageGraph } from '../../lib/schema';

const tools = toolsByCategory('sewing');
const title = 'Sewing Calculators: Fabric & Seams';
const description =
  'Free sewing calculators for fabric yardage (garments, curtains, upholstery) and seam allowance or pattern grading helpers. Plan cuts before you buy.';
const jsonLd = collectionPageGraph({
  name: title,
  description,
  path: '/sewing/',
  crumbs: [
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Sewing', path: '/sewing/' },
  ],
});
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/sewing/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Sewing' }]} />
    <h1>Sewing calculators</h1>
    <p class="takeaway">
      <strong>Key takeaway:</strong> Estimate fabric from project dimensions and fabric width, then refine cut sizes with
      seam allowance and ease helpers—before you commit to a bolt cut.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The <a href="/tools/fabric-yardage-calculator/">fabric yardage calculator</a> is for shopping lists:
        finished width and length, fabric width, waste, and optional pattern repeat. The
        <a href="/tools/seam-allowance-calculator/">seam allowance calculator</a> converts finished measurements
        to cut sizes, grades a measurement between sizes, or adds wearing ease. Neither tool replaces a full
        pattern; both keep arithmetic local in your browser so you can iterate on curtain lengths, tablecloth
        overhangs, or apparel ease without uploading files.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you are planning dress, curtain, or quilt-related yardage in words rather than in a form, read
        <a href="/guides/how-many-yards-of-fabric/">how many yards of fabric you need</a>. Quilters who crossed over
        from garment sewing often need binding and backing math next—see the
        <a href="/guides/how-much-quilt-binding-do-i-need/">quilt binding guide</a> and the
        <a href="/quilting/">quilting hub</a>. For seam conventions on patchwork, the
        <a href="/guides/half-square-triangle-math/">half-square triangle guide</a> explains unfinished vs finished
        sizes that affect how much fabric a block grid consumes.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tip: match the unit system on your pattern (inches vs centimeters) and write the fabric width from the bolt
        end, not from memory—quilting cotton, home-dec, and wide backing differ. Add waste for directional prints
        and nap; the fabric calculator’s waste field exists for that reason.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="tool-grid">
      {tools.map((t) => (
        <a class="tool-link" href={t.path}><h2>{t.title}</h2><p>{t.description}</p></a>
      ))}
    </div>
    <p>
      Guides: <a href="/guides/how-many-yards-of-fabric/">fabric yardage</a> ·
      <a href="/guides/">all guides</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
